<main><section class="page-hero legal-hero"><div class="site-container"><p class="section-kicker">LEGAL INFORMATION</p><span class="draft-badge">Draft — not yet in force</span><h1>Privacy notice.</h1><p>Version {{ config('sortd.legal.privacy_version') }}. This draft explains how the private Sortd test site is intended to handle information. It needs legal review before launch.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="site-container legal-grid"><nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#information">Information collected</a><a href="#purpose">How it is used</a><a href="#sharing">Sharing</a><a href="#security">Security</a><a href="#choices">Your choices</a><a href="#draft">Draft status</a></nav><article class="legal-content"><section id="information"><h2>Information collected</h2><p>Account sign-up asks for your name, email address and a South African mobile number. Using Sortd may also involve property and job details, photos, quotes and pro application information. The test site is for fake information only.</p></section><section id="purpose"><h2>How it is used</h2><p>Sortd uses account details to provide sign-in and verification, and job information to help match work with eligible pros, prepare quotes and track progress. Optional marketing consent is separate from account consent.</p></section><section id="sharing"><h2>Sharing</h2><p>Pros can see job information needed to quote, including the area name and roughly how far away the job is. A customer's street address and contact details are intended to be shared only with the pro whose quote is accepted. Address search uses Google Places: the text you type while searching for an address is sent to Google. A pro's work address is stored encrypted and is never shown to customers, who see only an area name. Providers used for sign-in, email and messaging may process the information needed to deliver those services.</p></section><section id="security"><h2>Security and retention</h2><p>Sortd uses access controls and other safeguards for account and job information. Retention periods and the full list of service providers will be detailed in the final notice. The private preview is not a place to store real personal information.</p></section><section id="choices"><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can choose whether to receive optional marketing. The final notice will explain how to request access, correction or deletion of your personal information and how to raise a privacy concern.</p></section><section id="draft"><h2>Draft status</h2><p>This notice is incomplete and will be reviewed before launch. See the <a wire:navigate.hover href="{{ route('terms') }}">Terms of service</a> for the current test site outline.</p></section></article></div></section></main>@include('pages.partials.footer')</div></x-layouts.app>
